ic Land — Swamp"},{"cmc":4.0,"color_identity":["W"],"colors":["W"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{W}{W}","name":"Wrath of God","oracle_id":"34515b16-c9a4-4f98-8c77-416a7a523407","oracle_text":"Destroy all creatures. They can't be regenerated.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2023-08-04","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it.","oracle_id":"049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If this creature gets enough -1/-1 counters put on it to cause its toughness to be 0 or less (or the damage marked on it to be lethal), modular will put a number of +1/+1 counters on the target artifact creature equal to the number of +1/+1 counters on this creature before it left the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6d9af084-cd5d-4242-b0f0-24a36d0a75d4","published_at":"2006-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each creature you don't control that dies causes a delayed triggered ability to trigger at the beginning of the next end step. If there are multiple such abilities, you can put them on the stack in any order. The creatures will return to the battlefield one at a time as each ability resolves. The last ability you put on the stack will be the first one to resolve.","oracle_id":"892c8fd1-9553-4ced-84ec-9fc35c314c76","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Grave Betrayal doesn't overwrite any previous colors or types. Rather, it adds another color and another creature type.","oracle_id":"892c8fd1-9553-4ced-84ec-9fc35c314c76","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature you don't control dies during the end step, that creature won't return to the battlefield until the beginning of the next end step.","oracle_id":"892c8fd1-9553-4ced-84ec-9fc35c314c76","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the creature card leaves the graveyard before the delayed triggered ability resolves, it won't return to the battlefield. This is also true if the card leaves the graveyard and returns to the graveyard before that ability resolves.","oracle_id":"892c8fd1-9553-4ced-84ec-9fc35c314c76","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the creature is normally colorless, it will simply be black. It won't be both black and colorless.","oracle_id":"892c8fd1-9553-4ced-84ec-9fc35c314c76","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In a multiplayer game, if more than one player controls a Grave Betrayal and a creature controlled by none of those players dies, each Grave Betrayal will create a delayed triggered ability at the beginning of the next end step. The first such ability to resolve will return the creature. Usually, this will be one controlled by the player furthest from the active player in turn order.","oracle_id":"892c8fd1-9553-4ced-84ec-9fc35c314c76","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The phrase \"with an additional +1/+1 counter on it\" means that the creature enters with one more +1/+1 counter than it would normally enter with. It doesn't keep any counters it had on it when it died.","oracle_id":"892c8fd1-9553-4ced-84ec-9fc35c314c76","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card in a graveyard has {X} in its mana cost, X is 0.","oracle_id":"a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If any abilities trigger on the creature entering the battlefield, those abilities resolve after you lose life. If losing life results in you losing the game, those abilities won't resolve.","oracle_id":"a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, the creature you control from Reanimate is exiled.","oracle_id":"a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The amount of life you lose is determined by the mana value of the card in your graveyard, not the creature once it's on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You lose life after the creature is already on the battlefield. Any abilities it has that interact with loss of life, such as that of Platinum Emperion, apply to that loss of life.","oracle_id":"a044474a-cd72-4e9d-bd8d-a08f2de9cdc0","published_at":"2025-09-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.","oracle_id":"b5f9920d-7af5-4876-8823-6efbf2b4d9b9","published_at":"2008-08-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
